{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "MadronichLayerColumns",
  "description": "Stage 2 of WRF-Chem's Madronich photolysis (phot_opt = 1): the layer-mean quantities SUBROUTINE subgrid derives from the interface column (chem/module_phot_mad.F:2446-2510, WRF v4.8.0) -- the layer temperature, the air, ozone and aerosol columns, the cloud optical depth, and the O2 column above each layer mid-point that the Schumann-Runge parameterization runs on.\n\nSCOPE, stated up front: this component is exact for a CLEAR column and only for a clear column. subgrid does two things -- it inserts extra levels inside cloud, and it forms layer means -- and only the second is written here. The insertion adds max(int(cloud dz 0.02), 1) levels per cloudy model layer, so `nlevel` is a function of the cloud field: 70, 72, 77 and 78 at the four dumped daytime calls of the reference run. An esm index set has a size fixed at load, so a grid whose SIZE is state-dependent cannot be expressed as one; representing the cloudy case needs either a fixed maximum grid with masked levels or an adaptive-grid discretization, and that is a design decision rather than a transcription. Where cloud is absent the insertion is a no-op, the regridded column IS the interface column, and everything below is exact -- which the test verifies against the one dumped daytime call whose column is completely clear.\n\nTwo of these are written as integrals rather than as the sums the Fortran spells. `vaer` is normalized by the column-integrated aerosol extinction. And `cvo2` -- which the Fortran builds by a downward recurrence from the model top, cvo2(L) = 0.2095 vair(L)/2 and cvo2(k) = cvo2(k+1) + 0.2095 (vair(k)+vair(k+1))/2 -- telescopes exactly to 0.2095 (column above interface k - vair(k)/2), the O2 column above the layer MID-POINT, which is what the Fortran's own comment says it is building. Writing it as the integral removes the recurrence entirely.\n\n`vo3` deserves a note: the Fortran gets it by calling trapez to interpolate the interface ozone onto zmid and then multiplying by dz. For a clear column zmid is the arithmetic mid-point of the two bounding interfaces, so that interpolation IS the arithmetic mean, and the layer ozone column is the trapezoidal one. Verified against the dump before this file was written."
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 69,
   "description": "Number of radiative-transfer layers (nlayer = nlevel-1). 69 for a clear column of the 60-level reference sounding."
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "MadronichLayerColumns": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/integral_lev_whole.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_to_top.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    }
   ],
   "subsystems": {
    "par": {
     "ref": "./madronich_parameters.esm"
    }
   },
   "variables": {
    "ze": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "km",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Radiative-transfer interface heights (photolysis_mad `z`), from MadronichColumnSetup. Supplied by the consumer; this component does not own it.",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ]
    },
    "t_node": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "default": 250.0,
     "description": "Temperature on the RT interfaces (`zt`), from MadronichColumnSetup.",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ]
    },
    "air_node": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "cm^-3",
     "default": 1e+19,
     "description": "Air number density on the RT interfaces (`zair`).",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ]
    },
    "o3_node": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "cm^-3",
     "default": 1000000000000.0,
     "description": "Ozone number density on the RT interfaces, AFTER the 325 DU rescaling.",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ]
    },
    "aer_node": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1/km",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Aerosol extinction on the RT interfaces.",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ]
    },
    "cloud_node": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1/km",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Cloud extinction on the RT interfaces.",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ]
    },
    "dz": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "km",
     "description": "Layer thickness, z(i+1)-z(i) (grid: column_cell_thickness).",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "zmid": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "km",
     "description": "Layer mid-point altitude (grid: column_cell_center). This is `zmid`, the altitude srband tests against 20 km and the altitude every layer-mean optical quantity refers to.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "vt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Layer-mean temperature, (zt(lay+1)+zt(lay))/2. Drives the layer-mean ozone cross section ao3 and, above 200 nm, the Schumann-Runge fit.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "air_layer": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "cm^-3",
     "description": "Layer-mean air number density.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "vair": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "cm^-2",
     "description": "Vertical air column in the layer, dz 1e5 (zair(i+1)+zair(i))/2.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "o3_layer": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "cm^-3",
     "description": "Layer-mean ozone number density; equivalently trapez's interpolation of o3 onto zmid.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "vo3": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "cm^-2",
     "description": "Vertical ozone column in the layer.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "aer_layer": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1/km",
     "description": "Layer-mean aerosol extinction.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "vaer_raw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Layer aerosol optical depth before normalization, dz times the layer mean.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "aer_total": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Column-integrated aerosol extinction, the normalization denominator."
    },
    "vaer": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Layer aerosol optical depth NORMALIZED so the column sums to one. optics then multiplies it by the wavelength-dependent total aaer(kl) = 0.379 (340/lambda), so only the SHAPE of the aerosol profile survives from the model; its magnitude is the Elterman climatology, not the model's.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "cloud_layer": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1/km",
     "description": "Layer-mean cloud extinction.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "vcld": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Layer cloud optical depth, the layer-mean extinction times dz. Identically zero wherever this component is valid (see the description); the cloudy case needs the inserted grid that this component deliberately does not build.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "air_above": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "cm^-3 km",
     "description": "Air column from each interface to the model top, the integral of the layer-mean air over dz.",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ]
    },
    "cvo2": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "cm^-2",
     "description": "Vertical O2 column above the MID-POINT of each layer, 0.2095 (column above the interface - vair/2). srband's independent variable.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "z_sfc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "km",
     "description": "Lower boundary of the column, ze[1]: the free name the EarthSciDiscretizations column_nonuniform_1d integral rules match as the lower bound of a bottom-anchored integral (ESD #39)."
    },
    "z_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "km",
     "description": "Upper boundary of the column, ze[NLEV+1]: the free name the EarthSciDiscretizations column_nonuniform_1d integral rules match as the upper bound of a top-anchored integral (ESD #39)."
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "dz",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "column_cell_thickness",
      "bindings": {
       "ze": "ze"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "zmid",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "column_cell_center",
      "bindings": {
       "ze": "ze"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "vt",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "j"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "j": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        0.5,
        {
         "op": "+",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "t_node",
            "j"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "t_node",
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              "j",
              1
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      "args": [
       "t_node"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "air_layer",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "j"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "j": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        0.5,
        {
         "op": "+",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "air_node",
            "j"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "air_node",
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              "j",
              1
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      "args": [
       "air_node"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "vair",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "par.km_to_cm",
       "dz",
       "air_layer"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "o3_layer",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "j"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "j": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        0.5,
        {
         "op": "+",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "o3_node",
            "j"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "o3_node",
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              "j",
              1
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      "args": [
       "o3_node"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "vo3",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "par.km_to_cm",
       "dz",
       "o3_layer"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "aer_layer",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "j"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "j": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        0.5,
        {
         "op": "+",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "aer_node",
            "j"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "aer_node",
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              "j",
              1
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      "args": [
       "aer_node"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "vaer_raw",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "dz",
       "aer_layer"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "aer_total",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "integral",
      "args": [
       "aer_layer"
      ],
      "var": "lev",
      "lower": "z_sfc",
      "upper": "z_top"
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "vaer",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       "vaer_raw",
       "aer_total"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "cloud_layer",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "j"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "j": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        0.5,
        {
         "op": "+",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "cloud_node",
            "j"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "cloud_node",
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              "j",
              1
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      "args": [
       "cloud_node"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "vcld",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "cloud_layer",
       "dz"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "air_above",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "integral",
      "args": [
       "air_layer"
      ],
      "var": "lev",
      "lower": "lev_nodes",
      "upper": "z_top"
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "cvo2",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "j"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "j": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        "par.o2_fraction",
        {
         "op": "-",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "*",
           "args": [
            "par.km_to_cm",
            {
             "op": "index",
             "args": [
              "air_above",
              "j"
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "*",
           "args": [
            0.5,
            {
             "op": "index",
             "args": [
              "vair",
              "j"
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      "args": [
       "air_above",
       "vair"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "z_sfc",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "index",
      "args": [
       "ze",
       1
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "z_top",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "index",
      "args": [
       "ze",
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         "NLEV",
         1
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ],
